Legend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Edges
  ──▶ depends  consumer uses provider
  ──▶ governs  architect over component; mode advisor, arbiter or owner
  ──▶ deploys  deployer runs the app's deploys
  Request rule on an edge from A to B
  normal  delivered; B judges it
  auto    delivered with a trust note; B can act without asking you, still inside B's merge authority and refusals
  ask     held in Needs you
  never   refused
  a specific edge beats the all projects wildcard; an edge never grants deploy or merge permission by itself (deploy_rule and merge_authority do)
  Charter fields
  maturity         sets the default rules; the only charter field with an enforced effect
  accepts          your agent reads it every turn; every neighbour reads the first 40 characters
  refuses          same as accepts
  escalate         your agent reads it every turn
  purpose          in a worker's brief
  consumers        in a worker's brief
  needs            in a worker's brief, and in the Tools tab
  notes            in a worker's brief
  feature_requests shown only when another agent looks this node up
Charter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
accepts          New document sources, retrieval fixes, and schema changes that keep old ids working.
refuses          Anything that writes to the trading accounts; one-off client reports.
feature_requests Open an issue in the repo; the architect triages them every Monday.
